"<thinking>\n\n**Step A: Text Breakdown**\n\nLet's extract every major user need, implied feature, and technical or qualitative constraint from the text:\n\n1. \"The app will be available for Android and iOS devices.\"\n2. \"The app must be fully loaded and ready to use within a maximum of two seconds after starting.\"\n3. \"Offer football fans a central platform to stay comprehensively informed at all times.\"\n4. \"Users can display current football news of their favorite teams.\"\n5. \"Select preferred sports channels individually.\"\n6. \"Users can follow results of their favorite teams live via a live ticker.\"\n7. \"Extensive coverage of all leagues and competitions, both national and international.\"\n8. \"Detailed team and player information available at any time.\"\n9. \"Integration of live stream links from providers such as DAZN or Sky Sport, displayed as soon as the live broadcast begins.\"\n10. \"Compliance with transmission rights is maintained. Live streams only shown when rights are fulfilled in the country.\"\n11. \"Users can retrieve live results in real time.\"\n12. \"App includes an integrated live ticker module enabling retrieval and display of live data in real time.\"\n13. \"User interface allows direct access to app information.\"\n14. \"UI connects various modules that are managed and displayed together.\"\n15. \"Live ticker module communicates via the interface with the UI to display and update match data.\"\n16. \"Live data is retrieved via API from external server.\"\n17. \"Additional modules allow users to individually configure the app and connect their own interface to UI.\"\n18. \"App linked to notification system for current event notifications once function is activated.\"\n19. \"All modules and UI are fixed components, remain consistent despite server updates.\"\n20. \"Registration and login can be completed directly at app startup and are designed to be uncomplicated.\"\n21. \"Users can follow favorite clubs and receive notifications about news or results.\"\n22. \"Users can share news and reports via social media directly from the app.\"\n23. \"App functions reliably even with limited network coverage.\"\n24. \"App remains usable offline, even if connection is lost temporarily.\"\n25. \"Designed for up to 100,000 simultaneous users without loss of performance.\"\n26. \"App goes through thorough testing and support before release to detect and resolve malfunctions early.\"\n27. \"User feedback and app reviews are continuously evaluated for improvement.\"\n28. \"All personal data is processed in compliance with GDPR.\"\n\n**Step B: Requirement Extraction & Sorting**\n\nLet's now sort the extracted points into preliminary Functional and Non-Functional Requirements:\n\nFunctional Requirements Candidates:\n1. Android and iOS support (Deployment constraint, but more of NFR or Release Target; possibly note as a functional expectation for platform support)\n2. Show football news for favorite teams\n3. Select preferred sports channels\n4. Follow live results via ticker\n5. Support coverage for all leagues and competitions\n6. Display detailed team and player info\n7. Integrate live stream links from broadcasters, display when live\n8. Only show streams when rights are fulfilled in the country\n9. Real time live results access\n10. Real time live ticker retrieval\n11. UI gives direct information access\n12. UI and modules are integrated and managed together\n13. Live ticker module displays and updates match data\n14. Live data retrieved via external API\n15. Additional modules for user interface personalization/configuration\n16. Notification system for events/news\n17. Registration/login at app start, uncomplicated\n18. Users can follow clubs, get notifications\n19. Share news and reports via social media\n\nNon-Functional Requirements Candidates:\n1. Fully loaded and usable within 2 seconds\n2. App remains usable with limited network\n3. Offline usability when connection is lost\n4. Consistent modules/UI despite server updates\n5. Serve up to 100,000 users simultaneously without loss of performance\n6. Thorough testing/support before release\n7. Continuous improvement via feedback/app reviews\n8. GDPR-compliant personal data processing\n\n**Step C: De-duplication & Overlap Check**\n\n- \"Live ticker,\" \"real time results,\" and \"live data via API\" are related; consider a requirement about real-time live results via integrated live ticker using dynamic API.\n- Personalization (teams, clubs, channels) appears in several lines; must cover selection, configuration, and notification preferences.\n- \"Registration/login\" and \"uncomplicated onboarding\" are related. Articulate as a streamlined auth flow.\n- Notifications for news/events/results need grouping.\n- UI/integration/module separation mainly affects maintainability but also user access and consistency.\n- Offline, limited network, and high concurrent user load are distinct but related resilience/availability constraints.\n- GDPR and data privacy: emphasize distinctly.\n- Testing and continuous improvement: process-oriented, one requirement each.\n\n**Step D: BDD Planning**\n\nPersona(s):\n- Football app users (fans), with sub-roles: news readers, match followers, social sharers\n- System administrator (for NFRs/testing, out of scope for main user needs)\n\nBDD scenarios:\n- News selection/personalization: Given on team/channel selection screen, select items, When saved, Then feed is filtered accordingly.\n- Live ticker: Given viewing match, When match in progress, Then live updates visible in real time.\n- Live stream availability: Given live match is being broadcast, When user in a region with rights, Then live stream link is shown; When not in region, Then not shown.\n- Registration/login: Given new user, When app first started, Then registration/login available and simple.\n- Notifications: Given notifications enabled, When news or results for followed teams, Then push notification sent.\n- Offline usage: Given no connection, When open app, Then can still view last available data and core functions.\n- Performance: Given app is closed, When started, Then dashboard loads within 2 seconds.\n- High user load: Given match day, When 100,000 users online, Then no slowdown.\n- GDPR: Given registration/data input, When saved, Then processed per GDPR.\n- Testing process: Given release cycle, When update built, Then goes through defined QA process.\n- Social sharing: Given open news item, When share selected, Then choice of social network offered.\n\n**Step E: ID Assignment**\n\n- FR-001: Personalized news feed (teams and channels)\n- FR-002: Live ticker for favorite team results\n- FR-003: Full league/competition coverage\n- FR-004: Detailed team and player information\n- FR-005: Live stream links per broadcast availability and licensing\n- FR-006: Notification system for events/news/results\n- FR-007: Registration and login at app startup (simple)\n- FR-008: Social media sharing of news/reports\n- FR-009: User can personalize/configure modules and interface\n\n- NFR-001: App loads fully ready to use within 2 seconds\n- NFR-002: Resilient performance with limited network\n- NFR-003: Usable offline when connection lost\n- NFR-004: 100,000 users concurrent without loss of performance\n- NFR-005: Consistent modules and UI across server updates\n- NFR-006: Thorough testing/support process before release\n- NFR-007: Continuous evaluation of user feedback/app reviews\n- NFR-008: Personal data processed per GDPR\n- NFR-009: Android and iOS deployment\n\n</thinking>"